; One diagnostic, on the child that crosses the set's ceiling — the line
; to delete — with that child's own positional step as its path, exactly
; where the per-head code lands. One report per crossing, not one per
; child past it: the emit fires on the transition from `max-children` to
; `max-children + 1`.
;
; The code is `positional_too_many`, reused rather than appended to. The
; child that trips a ceiling is the same kind of thing at either level,
; and the suppression rule means a host never sees both on one span — so
; nothing has to read prose to tell the levels apart. The message carries
; the set (`[buffer | sampler | texture]`) where the per-head one carries
; the head.
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code positional_too_many :severity err :path [entry sampler]))
